abstract: >-
  Sahbi conjectured that the k-independence number and the upper k-star-forming number agree on
  bipartite graphs, and in particular on chain graphs, and asked whether they agree for k = 3 on
  triangle-free graphs. For every k >= 3 we give a connected bipartite graph on 3k + 3 vertices with
  k-independence number 2k + 2 and a minimal k-star-forming set of size 3k. On chain graphs, however,
  the two numbers agree for every k. Both results are formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib.
